   "evidence": "Both are in scope: `code/.../Diffractive/Kinematics.lean:87` `def xi (i : Invariants) : \u211d := i.Dq / i.Pq` and `code/.../Exclusive/Kinematics/Basic.lean:76` `noncomputable def xiSkew ...`, the latter reachable via the `public import` at line 9 and via `ofExcl`, whose argument is an `ExclKinematics`. Substituting \u03be = 2\u03b7/(1+\u03b7) into `-\u03be\u00b2M\u00b2/(1-\u03be)` gives `-4\u03b7\u00b2M\u00b2/(1-\u03b7\u00b2)`, so the two forms are not interchangeable. Roadmap Convention 1 (Diffraction/README.md:107-111) names this exact trap.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Scattering/DIS/Diffractive/Kinematics.lean",
   "fix": "State in the `tMinElastic` docstring that `xi` is the momentum fraction lost by the target, `Invariants.xi = \u0394\u00b7q/P\u00b7q`, and explicitly not the skewness `ExclKinematics.xiSkew`.",
   "issue": "`tMinElastic (M xi : \u211d)` takes a bare real and its docstring says only \"at fixed `\u03be`\", but the file publicly imports `Exclusive.Kinematics.Basic`, which exposes a second, different \u03be: `ExclKinematics.xiSkew` (BMK's skewness \u03b7, Exclusive/Kinematics/Basic.lean:76). The formula `-\u03be\u00b2M\u00b2/(1-\u03be)` is valid only for the momentum-fraction-loss \u03be (`Invariants.xi`); for the skewness the same boundary is `-4\u03b7\u00b2M\u00b2/(1-\u03b7\u00b2)`, so `tMinElastic M (K.xiSkew g)` type-checks and is numerically wrong.",
   "line": 208
  }
